Looking at the code fragments, I can see that the Hexi library provides binary stream functionality for serialization. Based on the examples, I need to:

1. Create a buffer and adaptor
2. Create a binary stream with the adaptor
3. Write the raw header using `put()` or stream operator
4. Serialize the UserData structure using `serialise()`
5. Return the buffer

Here's the complete file:

```cpp
#include <hexi/hexi.h>
#include <vector>
#include <cstdint>

struct UserData {
    uint32_t user_id;
    std::string name;

    void serialise(auto& adaptor) {
        adaptor(user_id, name);
    }
};

std::vector<uint8_t> write_and_serialise_packet(uint32_t header, const UserData& data) {
    // Create a vector buffer to hold the serialized data
    std::vector<uint8_t> buffer;

    // Create a buffer adaptor for the vector
    hexi::buffer_adaptor adaptor(buffer);

    // Create a binary stream with the adaptor
    hexi::binary_stream stream(adaptor);

    // Write the raw header (uint32_t)
    stream.put(header);

    // Serialize the UserData structure
    stream.serialise(data);

    // Return the buffer containing all serialized data
    return buffer;
}
```

