output.text:
Looking at the code fragments and understanding how `hexi::detail::intrusive_storage` works based on the test examples, I can implement the three required functions:

```cpp
#include <hexi/detail/intrusive_storage.h>
#include <vector>
#include <cstdint>

template<size_t block_size = 1024>
std::vector<uint8_t> preview_data_without_consuming(const hexi::detail::intrusive_storage<block_size>& storage, size_t bytes_to_preview) {
    // Create a copy of the storage to preview without modifying the original
    auto storage_copy = storage;

    // Limit preview size to available data
    size_t preview_size = std::min(bytes_to_preview, storage_copy.size());

    // Create result vector and read from the copy
    std::vector<uint8_t> result(preview_size);
    if (preview_size > 0) {
        storage_copy.read(result.data(), preview_size);
    }

    return result;
}

template<size_t block_size = 1024>
struct BufferStatus {
    size_t readable_size;
    size_t free_space;
};

template<size_t block_size = 1024>
BufferStatus<block_size> check_buffer_status(const hexi::detail::intrusive_storage<block_size>& storage) {
    BufferStatus<block_size> status;

    // Get the current readable size
    status.readable_size = storage.size();

    // Calculate free space (capacity - current size)
    // intrusive_storage has a fixed capacity equal to block_size
    status.free_space = block_size - status.readable_size;

    return status;
}

template<size_t block_size = 1024>
void reset_buffer(hexi::detail::intrusive_storage<block_size>& storage) {
    // Clear the buffer by reading all available data
    // This effectively resets both read and write offsets
    size_t current_size = storage.size();
    if (current_size > 0) {
        storage.skip(current_size);
    }

    // Alternatively, we could create a new instance and assign it
    // storage = hexi::detail::intrusive_storage<block_size>();
}
```

**Explanation:**

1. **`preview_data_without_consuming`**: 
   - Creates a copy of the storage buffer to avoid modifying the original
   - Limits the preview size to the actual available data
   - Reads from the copy into a vector and returns it
   - The original storage remains unchanged

2. **`check_buffer_status`**:
   - Returns the readable size using `storage.size()` (number of bytes that can be read)
   - Calculates free space as the difference between the block size (capacity) and current size
   - Based on the tests, `intrusive_storage` has a fixed capacity equal to its template parameter

3. **`reset_buffer`**:
   - Resets the buffer by skipping all readable data, which advances the read pointer to match the write pointer
   - This effectively empties the buffer and resets it to initial state
   - An alternative approach (commented) would be to assign a new instance

