Looking at the code fragments, I can see that `hexi::file_buffer` is used to read and write binary data from/to files. Based on the test examples, I can see that:

1. `file_buffer` has a constructor that takes a `std::filesystem::path`
2. It has `read()` and `write()` template methods for reading/writing primitive types
3. The library handles binary I/O operations

Here's the complete implementation:

```cpp
#include <hexi/file_buffer.h>
#include <cstdint>
#include <filesystem>

uint32_t read_uint32_from_file(const std::filesystem::path& file_path) {
    hexi::file_buffer buffer(file_path);
    uint32_t value = 0;
    buffer.read(&value, sizeof(value));
    return value;
}

void write_uint32_to_file(const std::filesystem::path& file_path, uint32_t value) {
    hexi::file_buffer buffer(file_path);
    buffer.write(&value, sizeof(value));
}
```

