   - Creates a `hexi::file_buffer` object with the given file path
   - Uses `buffer.write(&value, sizeof(value))` to write the `uint32_t` value as binary data to the file

The `file_buffer` class from the Hexi library handles the low-level file I/O operations, and we simply need to call its `read()` and `write()` methods with a pointer to our data and the size to read/write.

