Looking at the code fragments, I can see that `hexi::pmc::stream_base` provides methods to interact with the underlying buffer. From the test cases, I can see:

1. `stream.size()` - gets the size of the stream buffer
2. `stream.empty()` - checks if the stream is empty
3. `stream.state()` - gets the stream state (returns `hexi::stream_state`)

Here's the complete implementation:

```cpp
#include <hexi/pmc/stream_base.h>
#include <hexi/shared.h>

size_t get_stream_size(const hexi::pmc::stream_base& stream) {
    return stream.size();
}

bool is_stream_empty(const hexi::pmc::stream_base& stream) {
    return stream.empty();
}

struct StreamInfo {
    hexi::stream_state state;
    size_t buffer_size;
    bool is_empty;
};

StreamInfo get_stream_state_info(const hexi::pmc::stream_base& stream) {
    StreamInfo info;
    info.state = stream.state();
    info.buffer_size = stream.size();
    info.is_empty = stream.empty();
    return info;
}
```

