Looking at the code fragments, I can see how the `hexi::pmc::buffer_adaptor` class is used. Based on the test cases, I can implement the required functions:

```cpp
#include <hexi/pmc/buffer_adaptor.h>
#include <vector>
#include <cstdint>

void write_data_to_buffer(hexi::pmc::buffer_adaptor<std::vector<std::byte>>& buffer, uint32_t value, const void* data, std::size_t length) {
    // Write the integer value first
    buffer.write(&value, sizeof(value));

    // Write the byte array
    buffer.write(data, length);
}

void read_data_from_buffer(hexi::pmc::buffer_adaptor<std::vector<std::byte>>& buffer, uint32_t& value, void* data, std::size_t length) {
    // Read the integer value first
    buffer.read(&value, sizeof(value));

    // Read the byte array
    buffer.read(data, length);
}

struct BufferInfo {
    std::size_t size;
    std::size_t free_space;
};

BufferInfo get_buffer_info(hexi::pmc::buffer_adaptor<std::vector<std::byte>>& buffer) {
    BufferInfo info;

    // Get the current size of the buffer (available data to read)
    info.size = buffer.size();

    // Get the free space available in the buffer
    // For vector-based buffer_adaptor, free() method returns available space
    info.free_space = buffer.free();

    return info;
}
```

**Explanation:**

1. **`write_data_to_buffer`**: 
   - Uses `buffer.write(&value, sizeof(value))` to write the uint32_t value to the buffer
   - Uses `buffer.write(data, length)` to write the byte array to the buffer
   - The write operations append data to the buffer

2. **`read_data_from_buffer`**:
   - Uses `buffer.read(&value, sizeof(value))` to read the uint32_t value from the buffer
   - Uses `buffer.read(data, length)` to read the byte array from the buffer
   - The read operations consume data from the buffer and advance the read pointer

3. **`get_buffer_info`**:
   - Uses `buffer.size()` to get the current size (amount of data available to read)
   - Uses `buffer.free()` to get the free space available in the buffer
   - Returns both values in a `BufferInfo` struct

