Looking at the code fragments and the Hexi library API, I need to implement two functions that work with `buffer_write_adaptor` and `buffer_read_adaptor`. Based on the examples, I can see:

1. `write()` - writes data to the buffer
2. `free()` - checks available space in the buffer
3. `size()` - returns the current size of data in the buffer
4. `read()` - reads data from the buffer
5. `empty()` - checks if buffer is empty

Here's the complete implementation:

```cpp
#include <hexi/pmc/buffer_read_adaptor.h>
#include <hexi/pmc/buffer_write_adaptor.h>
#include <vector>
#include <cstdint>

std::size_t write_multiple_chunks(const std::vector<std::vector<uint8_t>>& chunks) {
    // Create a vector to hold the buffer
    std::vector<uint8_t> buffer;

    // Create a write adaptor
    hexi::pmc::buffer_write_adaptor<std::vector<uint8_t>> write_adaptor(buffer);

    // Write each chunk, checking available space before each write
    for (const auto& chunk : chunks) {
        if (chunk.empty()) {
            continue;
        }

        // Check available space before writing
        // free() returns the available space in the buffer
        std::size_t available = write_adaptor.free();

        // Write the chunk (the vector will automatically grow if needed)
        write_adaptor.write(chunk.data(), chunk.size());
    }

    // Return the total size written
    return write_adaptor.size();
}

std::vector<uint8_t> read_partial_data(const std::vector<uint8_t>& buffer, std::size_t chunk_size) {
    // Create a copy of the buffer for reading
    std::vector<uint8_t> read_buffer = buffer;

    // Create a read adaptor
    hexi::pmc::buffer_read_adaptor<std::vector<uint8_t>> read_adaptor(read_buffer);

    // Vector to store all read data
    std::vector<uint8_t> result;

    // Read until buffer is empty
    while (!read_adaptor.empty()) {
        // Check remaining data size
        std::size_t remaining = read_adaptor.size();

        // Determine how much to read in this iteration
        std::size_t to_read = std::min(chunk_size, remaining);

        // Create temporary buffer for this chunk
        std::vector<uint8_t> temp(to_read);

        // Read the chunk
        read_adaptor.read(temp.data(), to_read);

        // Append to result
        result.insert(result.end(), temp.begin(), temp.end());
    }

    return result;
}
```

This implementation:

1. **`write_multiple_chunks`**:
   - Creates a `buffer_write_adaptor` wrapping a `std::vector<uint8_t>`
   - Iterates through each chunk in the input vector
   - Checks available space using `free()` before each write (though the vector will grow automatically)
   - Writes each chunk using `write()`
   - Returns the final buffer size using `size()`

2. **`read_partial_data`**:
   - Creates a copy of the input buffer and wraps it with `buffer_read_adaptor`
   - Continuously reads chunks of data until the buffer is empty
   - Uses `size()` to check remaining data after each read
   - Reads `chunk_size` bytes at a time (or less if remaining data is smaller)
   - Accumulates all read data into a result vector
   - Returns the complete data read from the buffer

